{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-11 04:07:45 UTC] [Agent: Codex] [Project: fix_read_recent_project_resolution] Localized root cause: explicit `project` parameter resolves only via JSON config (`config/projects/*.json`) and ignores database-registered projects; `query_entries` also fails to pass explicit_project into `resolve_logging_context`, so it falls back to `.scribe/docs/dev_plans/<slug>/PROGRESS_LOG.md` in current repo. | category=investigation; reasoning={\"how\": \"Patch `shared/logging_utils.resolve_logging_context` to resolve explicit_project via `storage_backend.fetch_project()` first (parse `docs_json`), then fallback to legacy config; update `tools/query_entries.py` to pass explicit_project from request config.\", \"what\": \"Constraint: must use StorageBackend abstraction (no direct SQL) and avoid replacement modules.\", \"why\": \"Need deterministic cross-repo project resolution for `read_recent`/`query_entries`.\"}; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/fix_read_recent_project_resolution/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-11T04:07:45.994377+00:00_6aabe420", "timestamp": "2026-01-11T04:07:45.994404+00:00"}
