{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-11 04:10:30 UTC] [Agent: Codex] [Project: fix_read_recent_project_resolution] Implemented fix: `resolve_logging_context` now resolves explicit project names via `storage_backend.fetch_project()` (with `docs_json` parsing) before falling back to legacy JSON config; `query_entries` now passes request `project` through as `explicit_project` for correct log path selection. Added regression tests; targeted pytest run passed. | confidence=0.85; deliverables=[\"shared/logging_utils.py\", \"tools/query_entries.py\", \"tests/test_logging_utils.py\", \"tests/test_query_entries_explicit_project_resolution.py\"]; reasoning={\"how\": \"Refactored session/explicit project resolution in `shared/logging_utils.resolve_logging_context` to prefer `fetch_project()`; updated `tools/query_entries.py` to pass explicit_project; added unit tests to lock behavior; ran targeted pytest.\", \"what\": \"Constraints: no replacement modules; use StorageBackend abstraction (no direct SQL); keep legacy config fallback intact.\", \"why\": \"Explicit project targeting must work for cross-repo projects stored in the DB; otherwise `read_recent(project=...)`/`query_entries(project=...)` silently read the wrong repo/project.\"}; tests=pytest -q tests/test_logging_utils.py::test_resolve_logging_context_explicit_project_uses_storage_backend tests/test_query_entries_explicit_project_resolution.py; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/fix_read_recent_project_resolution/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-11T04:10:30.741374+00:00_56bfc319", "timestamp": "2026-01-11T04:10:30.741403+00:00"}
{"op": "commit", "ref_id": "2026-01-11T04:10:30.741374+00:00_56bfc319", "timestamp": "2026-01-11T04:10:30.752518+00:00"}
{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-11 04:10:58 UTC] [Agent: Codex] [Project: fix_read_recent_project_resolution] User requested restoration of the removed WAL-mode isolation comment; update comment to match new implementation (StorageBackend.fetch_project) without reverting to direct SQL. | value={\"reasoning\":{\"why\":\"Maintain important historical context in code comments per user request.\",\"what\":\"Constraint: comment must remain accurate after refactor (we now use StorageBackend.fetch_project, not backend._fetchone / direct SQL). \",\"how\":\"Re-add the comment near session project resolution, rewritten to describe the current approach and the WAL-mode isolation risk it addresses; re-run targeted tests.\"}}; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/fix_read_recent_project_resolution/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-11T04:10:58.869815+00:00_910ddc55", "timestamp": "2026-01-11T04:10:58.869842+00:00"}
